# README screenshots (just readme-screenshots): raw 2x captures into artifacts/readme-screenshots; the recipe downscales
# them into docs/images. Projects live under the neutral /tmp/MainframeProjects (no user paths on screen): the recipe
# links Examples/Demo there and the workflow part creates MyGame there.
wait 30
# 1. The Project Manager with a few recent projects.
recent-project /tmp/MainframeProjects/Demo Demo 0.2
recent-project /tmp/MainframeProjects/SpaceMiner SpaceMiner 26
recent-project /tmp/MainframeProjects/PuzzleBox PuzzleBox 120
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-project-manager
# 2. The Demo's Basic 3D scene (the project's main scene opens with it): a light selected, debug lines filtered out, the Play tooltip showing.
open-project /tmp/MainframeProjects/Demo
wait-for project 300
wait 40
click #level-debug
collapse Ring
select Lights/WarmSpot
camera -0.3 0.9 -0.8 8.8 -18 -16
move #play
wait 60
capture editor
# 2b. Joints (ADR 0211): the Physics 3D rope bridge with a hinge selected (its axis, limit arc and angle in the
# selection colour, a line to each plank) and its Rebuild / Swap A/B buttons; then the Animation 3D character's
# Create physical skeleton (ADR 0212): its simulator deleted and created again from the Skeleton3D inspector (undone).
click #tool-select
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Scenes/physics_3d.mscene
wait 20
select Bridge/Hinge5
camera -4.3 2.2 -5 1.6 -24 -14
clear-output
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-joints
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Scenes/animation_3d.mscene
wait 20
select Crew/Armature/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D
key Delete
wait 5
select Crew/Armature
inspector-header skeleton-physical
camera 0 0.95 0 2.4 25 -8
clear-output
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-physical-skeleton
key Z cmd
wait 3
key Z cmd
wait 3
click #tool-translate
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Scenes/basic_3d.mscene
wait 10
# 3. The create dialog: a favourite, a recent type (added and undone), a search and a description.
move 800 500
key A cmd
wait 5
search Omni
pick OmniLight3D
accept
wait 5
key Z cmd
wait 5
key A cmd
wait 5
favorite MeshInstance3D
favorite RigidBody3D
search Body3D
pick RigidBody3D
click 900 640 # the description pane: the search field's focus tooltip goes away
wait 30
capture editor-add-node
cancel
wait 5
state
# 3b. Viewport tools (G7). Box selection: the floor, the plinth and the camera locked (the Scene panel's lock), the Ring's
# meshes selected by a first box, a second one held with Shift (the rectangle shows) while the move gizmo sits at their
# median.
expand Ring
lock Floor
lock Plinth
lock Camera
camera -0.3 0.9 -0.8 8.8 -18 -16
command gizmo.translate
pivot median
box-select 520 300 1000 600
wait 20
box-select 1010 260 1130 420 shift hold
wait 20
clear-output
wait 5
capture editor-box-select
mouse-up
wait 10
# Range handles: the blue omni light's range, dragged in from 7 m; the mouse rests on the handle (its label shows).
command gizmo.select
select Lights/Blue
camera -1 1 1 17 -25 -20
wait 10
handle-drag 0 -40 0 20
wait 20
clear-output
wait 5
capture editor-range-handles
command edit.undo
wait 5
# The resource row's More menu on the Box's inline mesh.
select Ring/Box
wait 10
res-menu Mesh
wait 20
clear-output
wait 5
capture editor-resource-menu
cancel
wait 5
# Simulate the physics scene: the Dropper's crates fall in the editor's view; the Pusher's inspector is live and read-only.
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Scenes/physics_3d.mscene
wait 20
select Pusher
simulate start
wait 150
move 800 500
wait 10
clear-output
wait 5
capture editor-simulate
simulate stop
wait 10
command file.close
wait 10
command edit.undo # the three locks of basic_3d
command edit.undo
command edit.undo
wait 5
# 3c. Animated sprites (ADR 0223/0224): the Demo's Sprites 2D scene with the showcase hero selected and its SpriteFrames
# editor in the inspector (the animation list, the frame strip with thumbnails); then the Select Frames dialog slicing
# the hero sheet into a 4x4 grid with the run row picked.
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Scenes/sprites_2d.mscene
wait 20
select Showcase
clear-output
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-sprite-frames
sheet-slicer Assets/Sprites2D/hero.png 4 4 0,1 1,1 2,1 3,1
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-sheet-slicer
cancel
wait 5
command file.close
wait 10
# 3e. Navigation (G3a): the Demo's Navigation 2D scene with Visible Navigation on (the baked grid's solid cells, the dashed
# mud, the region outline) and its NavigationGrid2D selected: the inspector's Bake / Clear buttons and status line.
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Scenes/navigation_2d.mscene
wait 20
select Grid
clear-output
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-navigation
command file.close
wait 10
# 3d. Crash reporting (G15): a played game's crash as one Output row, expanded to its frames (the game's frame links to
# its source, engine frames are muted), with the report, copy and frame buttons; then the editor's own next-start
# crash dialog with a recovery copy of the open scene (closed again: the sample report is marked handled).
clear-output
crash-row
move 800 500
wait 20
capture editor-crash
crash-dialog
wait 20
capture editor-crash-dialog
click #cr-close
wait 10
clear-output
# 3e. Export (G5): File › Export… on the Demo's presets (Windows, macOS, Linux, Linux server) with the server preset
# selected: a folder export without the music, so its scenes' music references warn.
command file.export
wait 10
export select 3
move 900 600
wait 20
capture editor-export
export close
wait 5
# 4. Audio: the sound designer on a Demo ZzFX preset, then the Demo's song in a song tab (the Lead clip in the piano
# roll). Paths are relative to the checkout: the project is open under its real path.
inspect Examples/Demo/Assets/Audio/Sfx/explosion.mres
wait 10
clear-output
move 800 500
wait 10
capture editor-sound-designer
inspector-header inspector-close
open Examples/Demo/Assets/Music/demo_loop.msong
wait 10
song select 1
move 1500 700
wait 20
capture editor-song
# The built-in effects: the Channel EQ on the master with its curve; then the Browser and the mixer's insert slots
# (undone again: the Demo's song stays as it is on disk).
song insert master eq lowCutOn=1 lowCutFreq=60 peak2Freq=900 peak2Gain=3 peak3Freq=3000 peak3Gain=-4 peak3Q=2.5 highShelfGain=2.5
song insert 1 compressor threshold=-24 ratio=3
song fx-window master 0
move 1500 700
wait 20
capture editor-song-effects
song fx-close
song browser on
song browser-toggle vst
song browser-toggle vsti
song pane mixer
wait 20
capture editor-song-browser
song browser-toggle vst
song browser-toggle vsti
song browser off
song pane roll
command edit.undo
command edit.undo
command edit.undo
command edit.undo
wait 5
# The wavetable synth on the Lead track with a factory preset (stacked wavetables, LFO 1 in the editor), playing so the
# modulated knobs show their live dots; undone again.
song synth 1
song synth-preset 1 Evolving Pad
song synth-page osc 4
song play
move 1500 700
wait 90
capture editor-song-synth
song stop
song synth-close
command edit.undo
command edit.undo
wait 5
# 5. Video mode: the recipe's narrated Physics 2D recording (build/readme-video-clip.sh) with its silences and filler
# words cut and a transcript, the playhead stopped at 2.8 s as the bodies fall through the pegs. base.en (the default,
# 148 MB on first use) because tiny.en's looser word timings leave cut words unstruck in the transcript.
mode video
open /tmp/MainframeProjects/Recordings/demo.mp4
wait-for video-jobs 60
wait 10
command video.detect_silence
wait-for video-jobs 60
wait 10
video set whisper-model base.en
command video.transcribe
wait-for video-jobs 900
wait 10
command video.remove_fillers
wait 10
command video.play
wait-for video-position 2.8 60
command video.play
wait 20
move 1500 700
wait 20
capture editor-video
# Save the edit (Save As defaults to Recordings/demo.mfcut) so closing the tab asks nothing and Play below has nothing
# unsaved to write.
command file.save_as
wait 10
accept
wait 10
command file.close
wait 10
mode game
wait 10
# 6. The game workflow: create MyGame, add an [Export] property to its C#, Build & Reload, play it.
command project.new
wait 10
new-project /tmp/MainframeProjects MyGame
wait 30 # the .NET SDK check enables Create
click #np-create
wait-for project 300
wait 20
clear-output
replace-in-file MyGame/Src/Spinner.cs =\s45f; = 45f;\n\n/// <summary>Bobbing height, in metres.</summary>\n[Export(Range = "0,10,0.1")]\npublic float Wobble { get; set; } = 2.5f;
command project.build_reload
wait 3
wait-for idle 120
wait 10
select Spinner
camera 0 0.6 0 4.6 -38 -18
play-args --hidden
wait-for playing 120
wait 30
move 800 500
wait 10
capture editor-game-project
# 6b. The Profiler tab (G10) on the running MyGame: about 2 s streamed over the editor link, the slowest frame selected.
profile tab
profile record
wait-for profiled 120 60
profile slowest
profile pause
move 800 500
wait 10
capture editor-profiler
profile stop
profile output
command play.stop
wait-for stopped 30
quit
